    "created_at": "2021-09-17T09:36:33Z",
    "updated_at": "2021-09-17T09:36:33Z",
    "body": "I think it's fine to discuss here. The original issue was more pressing when `fetch()` and `<script type=\"module\">` didn't send credentials for same-origin requests, but that's no longer the case.\r\n\r\nHowever, a generic \"don't send credentials for this request\" attribute/value still seems like a good idea to me.\r\n\r\n`credentials=omit` would clash weirdly with `crossorigin=use-credentials`, although we could deprecate `crossorigin=use-credentials` in favour of `crossorigin` (which means use CORS) and `credentials` which controls credential sending.",
    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
    "pin": null,
    "reactions": {
      "url": "https://api.github.com/repos/whatwg/html/issues/comments/921655933/reactions",
