    "created_at": "2021-09-20T11:08:37Z",
    "updated_at": "2021-09-20T11:08:37Z",
    "body": "To 1, both `credentials=same-origin` and `credentialless` are origin- not site-bound. I think that's still a boundary that's going to be interesting to control as we make more collective progress to limit access to cross-site (third-party) credentials.\r\n\r\nYour suggestions for 2 and 3 seem reasonable to me as well.\r\n\r\nRegarding `omit`, I didn't think about the performance implications, which I suppose would also flow through to the cache? If we have `same-origin`, I think I agree that `omit` is of pretty limited usefulness and could be a potential footgun. I wouldn't be opposed to adding it later if that simplified the story.\r\n\r\n(Note, though, that I'm not sure what the priority of any of this actually is. It doesn't seem like a lot of effort, given that we already have the ductwork in place for things like `referrerpolicy` to have per-request effect. Perhaps @slightlyoff can weigh in with some motivating use cases that could help me figure out how this stacks up to other things we could be spending time on?)",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "pin": null,
    "reactions": {
